# Function Descriptions

Add a short description directly above every function — including helpers, handlers, hooks, and methods. Keep it to **1–2 lines max**.

## Guidelines

- State **what the function does**, not how it does it
- Use plain language; avoid jargon and implementation details
- Skip descriptions only for trivial one-liners where the name is fully self-explanatory (e.g. `getId`)

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — missing description
export async function uploadDocument(file: File, orgId: string) {
  ...
}

// ❌ BAD — too long or redundant
/** Validates the uploaded file, checks org permissions, uploads to Cloudinary, and saves metadata to the database */
export async function uploadDocument(file: File, orgId: string) {
  ...
}

// ✅ GOOD
/** Uploads a document to Cloudinary and saves its metadata for the org. */
export async function uploadDocument(file: File, orgId: string) {
  ...
}

// ✅ GOOD — hook
/** Returns the current upload progress and cancel handler for a file. */
function useUploadProgress(fileId: string) {
  ...
}
```
